| info = 
*Cast {{A|Light Verse}} and/or {{A|Dark Verse}} to fill in <u>'''2'''</u> pages that complete the '''Final Verse'''. Cannot be cast without two pages. Once the story is written, Dante fulfills the narrative by expending {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] on cast, which grants him <u>'''1'''</u> second of [[Invulnerability]] during casting and materializes one of four stories based on page order: '''Triumph''', '''Tragedy''', '''Wordwarden''', or '''Pageflight''', while removing both pages from the storybook display above the ability icons. Each story lasts for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''30 / 35 / 40 / 45''' seconds with a range of {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''15 / 20 / 25 / 30''' meters.
**The specific story ability icon appears above the storybook display when two pages are filled, with the pages visually glowing.
**Replace filled pages from the right to left by recasting Light or Dark Verses to create the desired story combination.
**Stories with active duration appear as ability buff timers beside Dante's hitpoints indicator.
*All stories can be recast while active.
*Casting Final Verse is a full-body animation that allows uninterrupted movement and parkour [[Maneuvers]].
*Dante's four favored chapters exhibit diverse effects involving protection, damage, summoning, and debuffing:
<div class="tabber-borderless" >
{{#tag:tabber|
{{!}}-{{!}}Triumph=
<div style="display:none;">'''Triumph'''<br></div>
*Written with two Light pages (default {{Keybind|2}} twice). '''Triumph''' bestows {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''2,250 / 2,500 / 2,750 / 3,000''' {{D|Overguard}} to Dante and his allies instantly in story range. While story duration is active, each kill or assisted kill made by Dante or his allies' weapons and abilities will regenerate their personal Overguard pools by {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''85 / 90 / 95 / 100''' points over <u>'''2'''</u> seconds. Overguard granted by Triumph is capped to {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''7,500 / 10,000 / 12,500 / 15,000''' total points.
*'''Ability Synergy:''' {{D|Overguard}} generated by {{A|Light Verse}} and Triumph are combined into a single pool with two separate maximum values affected by {{Stat|Ability Strength}}.
*Overguard from Triumph does not apply to rescued hostage in Rescue missions.

{{!}}-{{!}}Tragedy=
<div style="display:none;">'''Tragedy'''<br></div>
*Written with two Dark pages (default {{Keybind|3}} twice). '''Tragedy''' inflicts '''5,000 / 5,500 / 6,000 / 6,500''' {{D|Slash}} damage and {{D|Stagger}} to all enemies within story range and in [[Line of Sight]]. Enemies hit by Tragedy while debuffed with active {{D|Slash}}, {{D|Heat}}, or {{D|Toxin}} [[Status Effect]] will instantly receive the full damage from all damage ticks of the procs, multiplied by {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''2.25x / 2.5x / 2.75x / 3x'''; status effects are removed after inflicting damage.
**Damage is capped at <u>'''1'''</u> billion.
**Line-of-sight extends from Dante's model and from the player camera perspective.
***Enemies directly on screen, ran behind cover moments before the check, those already behind cover with partial body exposure, and standing on different height elevations are all eligible targets.
***Enemies to the sides and back of the camera view are detected via raycast lines to their head, torso and feet.
***Line-of-sight check is ignored for enemies within <u>'''5'''</u> meters of Dante.

{{!}}-{{!}}Wordwarden=
<div style="display:none;">'''Wordwarden'''<br></div>
*Written with first Light and last Dark pages (default {{Keybind|2}} then {{Keybind|3}}). '''Wordwarden''' summons <u>'''1'''</u> spectral Noctua companion that floats beside Dante and his allied Warframes in story range on cast for its story duration, attacking enemies struck by its warded player's weapons for <u>'''35% / 40% / 45% / 50%'''</u> of the original Noctua's damage amplified by its modded stats, including [[Status Chance]] for its equipped Physical and Elemental damage types.
**Wordwarden fires a homing Noctua energy projectile toward the warded player's target. The projectile has travel time and can be blocked by obstacles in the environment, unless modded with [[Punch Through]] stat.
***Projectile is '''not''' affected by [[Multishot]].
**Targets the enemy last struck by its warded player, firing a maximum of once every <u>'''0.333'''</u> seconds.
***Fire rate of <u>'''3'''</u> is '''not''' affected by fire rate bonuses.
**Will not use the [[Alternate Fire]] and thus cannot trigger [[:Category:Invocation Mods|Invocation Mods]].  Will also not trigger [[:Category:Canticle Mods|Canticle Mods]].
**Can trigger mods and Arcanes such as {{M|Archon Stretch}} (provided the Exalted Noctua has {{D|Electricity}} modded onto it) or {{Arcane|Secondary Encumber}}.
***{{M|Galvanized Shot}}'s damage bonus does not scale correctly. On direct hits and homing fragments, it acts like the base damage is '''200''' (rather than 125), regardless of ability strength. 
*'''Ability Synergy:'''
**Kills from Wordwarden Noctua [[Dante/Abilities#Passive|passively]] scan enemies into the [[Codex]]. Wordwarden Noctua also gains <u>'''50%'''</u> [[Status Chance]] against enemies that have been fully scanned.
**Wordwarden inherits [[Mods]] placed on {{Weapon|Noctua}} and splits page fragments on hit that charge the held {{A|Noctua}}'s alt-fire. 

{{!}}-{{!}}Pageflight=
<div style="display:none;">'''Pageflight'''<br></div>
*Written with first Dark and last Light pages (default {{Keybind|3}} then {{Keybind|2}}). '''Pageflight''' summons <u>'''3'''</u> spectral [[Paragrimm]]s with high [[Threat Level]] that fly around for the story duration and attack enemies within <u>'''30'''</u> meters, dealing {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''150 / 200 / 250 / 300''' {{D|Slash}} damage, status, and {{D|Stagger}}. Enemies hit by Paragrimms also receive {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''35% / 40% / 45% / 50%''' [[Status Chance]] vulnerability and {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''35% / 40% / 45% / 50%''' increased Status Damage for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''15 / 20 / 25 / 30''' seconds.
**Status chance vulnerability is multiplicative to other sources of status chance, increasing a weapon's total status chance after mods and other bonuses are applied. It does '''not''' increase Pageflight's {{D|Slash}} statuses per Paragrimm hit.
***Does '''not''' affect the number of statuses from forced status procs, such as those in many melee combos, {{Weapon|Epitaph}}'s cold proc on uncharged shot AoE, or {{Weapon|Daikyu}}'s impact proc on hit.
**Status damage increase is multiplicative to other sources of status damage.
**Enemies debuffed by the Paragrimms are visually surrounded by an upsurging double helix.
*Pageflight Paragrimms are summoned allies with diverse properties and behaviors:
**[[Invulnerable]] and intangible, able to phase through enemy attacks, solid entities and obstacles in the environment.
**Are affected by {{M|Summoner's Wrath}}, {{Arcane|Arcane Camisado}}, and {{Arcane|Theorem Infection}}.
***Slash status effects from the Paragrimms do not double dip on the Summoner's Wrath bonus, despite it being a faction damage bonus (bug).
**Fly above Dante when no enemies are detected in range, and return to him when farther away than range.
**Detect enemies in range without direct line-of-sight.
**Prefer striking different targets to apply status vulnerability, while able to focus their combined attacks on a lone enemy. Once all enemies in range are debuffed, the Paragrimms prioritize attacking enemies closest to Dante himself.
**Strike each target by flying through them, then encircling back along their flight path.
*'''Ability Synergy:''' Pageflight's status chance vulnerability increases {{A|Dark Verse}}'s {{D|Slash}} status stacks per hit.

